  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure 3.5 on page 52, 'Layered view for one sub-goal relating to ensuring Quality and Continuity of Care' (section 3.3). The sub-goal 'Comprehensive Needs Assessment' (systematic evaluation of a patient's complete health status, risks and care requirements) is realised by the outcome 'Integrated, Person-Centered Care'. In 'Q&CC Sub-goal #1 Implementation', five capabilities realise that outcome: Care Protocol Management, Task-Sharing Orchestration, Patient History Integration, Quality and Performance Monitoring, and Decision Support. These are realised by the product 'Integrated Shared Care Plan (SCP)', which four services serve: Care Protocol Management, Clinical Decision Support, Patient History Aggregation Service, and Care Coordination and Task. Those services are realised by or served from the components Knowledge Base Engine, Electronic Medical Record, Interoperability Layer, Access Control and Authentication, Lifelong Health Record and Client Registry. A 'Grouping' at the bottom, which these components access, holds the Client Registry, Health Worker Registry, Facility Registry, Terminology Server and Product Registry.",
